                    insight_renewal:        `The Renewal Venture: you closed the round AND kept the team, the founder and the mission intact. One focused model, control priced not just sold, the margin-makers funded, and inclusion designed into the cost structure — this is the venture Camille can actually scale.`,
                    insight_control:        `Funded, founder sidelined: you reached the €750k close but the 'professional CEO' clause and the dilution left Camille's control thin. Reviva exists because a parent wouldn't let her scale her idea — and you recreated that with an investor holding the exit.`,
                    insight_team:           `Funded on the team's back: the money is in but work-life sustainability and engagement are weak. Your two best technicians produce the margin — without them, refurbished volume and certification collapse, and the model with it.`,
                    insight_short:          `Short of the close: you didn't reach €750,000, so the term sheet lapses, ~40% of soft commitments evaporate, and Reviva enters distressed fundraising at a likely down-round. Re-examine the model focus and the financing stack.`,
                    insight_mission:        `Mission drift: you pitched inclusion as a slide. An impact fund underwrites cost structure, not feel-good lines — and a mission that's only marketing is the first casualty when margins tighten.`,
                    insight_burnout:        `Founder burnout risk: work-life sustainability stayed low. A 70-hour founder with a newborn is an existential risk to an early-stage venture, not an HR footnote. The target needed euros behind it.`,
                    insight_attrition:      `Attrition risk: team engagement stayed low. The weekend-shift driver and the two at-risk technicians were the real production function — leaving them unaddressed undermines the whole growth plan.`,
